"An Eerie Cave"
"The cave floor is smooth sandstone, but it has been scorched and blackened by

an unknown source of heat.  Thousands of tiny stalactites hang from the

ceiling, none of which would cause much damage if it fell.  The faint echo of

crashing waves is heard from the west, the same direction a hot breathy breeze

blows, heading out of the cave.  A dull roar reaches your ears from the east

out of the darkness, and a faint orange-red glow can be seen.

"
